281
00:14:32,022 --> 00:14:34,082
Black, dragon horse to 6-4.

282
00:14:35,962 --> 00:14:38,222
Kiriyama, fifth den has seven minutes left.

283
00:14:38,222 --> 00:14:40,222
Well, uh...

284
00:14:40,222 --> 00:14:41,102
Thank you for dinner.

285
00:14:48,062 --> 00:14:49,762
Ray, what are you doing on TV?

286
00:14:50,162 --> 00:14:51,582
I thought you were going to show me.

287
00:14:51,802 --> 00:14:52,682
You're too heavy.

288
00:14:53,482 --> 00:14:55,042
Aw, shoot. Guess I blew it.

289
00:14:55,322 --> 00:14:57,802
Crap. I didn't know Kiriyama was keeping it a secret.

290
00:14:59,902 --> 00:15:01,702
Huh? What's going on?

291
00:15:01,962 --> 00:15:03,342
Looks like your secret's out.

292
00:15:03,602 --> 00:15:05,702
Oh, hello. Great to see you.

293
00:15:05,702 --> 00:15:09,702
Well, if it isn't Takahashi-san, hey, you've gotten big.

294
00:15:12,002 --> 00:15:14,882
How are your old man and granddad doing these days?

295
00:15:15,202 --> 00:15:15,562
Good.

296
00:15:16,102 --> 00:15:17,042
They're both well, sir.

297
00:15:17,402 --> 00:15:19,382
They were fighting over Shogi again last night.

298
00:15:20,382 --> 00:15:21,702
Uh, so, uh...

299
00:15:21,702 --> 00:15:24,122
They wanted me to ask Kiriyama, fifth den a question.

300
00:15:25,262 --> 00:15:27,582
Oh, it's the NHK cup.

301
00:15:28,282 --> 00:15:30,222
So which part? I was watching it, too.

302
00:15:30,222 --> 00:15:32,802
Oh, this one.

303
00:15:35,022 --> 00:15:36,702
Black, Dragon Horse to 4-2.

304
00:15:38,522 --> 00:15:40,322
What do you think you're doing, Kiriyama?

305
00:15:40,942 --> 00:15:44,422
I have no idea if you went in for the killer to be killed with that move.

306
00:15:44,762 --> 00:15:46,962
Now that's a truly passionate commentary.

307
00:15:47,602 --> 00:15:49,162
My dad and grandpa both agreed.

308
00:15:49,362 --> 00:15:52,002
They were saying they didn't think that one move was the losing move.

309
00:15:52,642 --> 00:15:56,102
They just couldn't figure out why Nikaido 4-2 was getting so riled up over it.

310
00:15:56,102 --> 00:15:59,022
Same king. Black, Gold, General to 5-5.

311
00:15:59,042 --> 00:16:00,862
Actually, Nikaido was right.

312
00:16:01,222 --> 00:16:03,242
That move was what caused me to lose the match.

313
00:16:07,162 --> 00:16:10,502
My dad and grandpa didn't think that move was really all that bad.

314
00:16:11,342 --> 00:16:14,862
In fact, they said it felt like an aggressive move fitting of a young man.

315
00:16:15,662 --> 00:16:20,122
My opponent had me surrounded waiting for me to make a mistake, and I had nowhere to go.

316
00:16:20,122 --> 00:16:25,002
I thought, let's find out if moving this piece over here will be a mistake or not.

317
00:16:26,102 --> 00:16:28,062
Don't try to act cool, Kiriyama!

318
00:16:28,882 --> 00:16:31,102
If you really want to win, stick it out!

319
00:16:31,382 --> 00:16:32,962
Don't just attack, you've got to defend!

320
00:16:33,542 --> 00:16:35,602
Why the hell have you been acting so weird lately?

321
00:16:35,842 --> 00:16:37,842
Mr. Nikaido, we can't see the board!

322
00:16:38,182 --> 00:16:41,962
You used to be so much more careful and determined back in the 3rd Den League.

323
00:16:42,102 --> 00:16:46,162
You may be braver now, but it's made you overconfident and reckless, and you know it!

324
00:16:46,162 --> 00:16:47,582
Please, you've got to calm down!

325
00:16:48,122 --> 00:16:49,942
Do you hear me, Kiriyama?

326
00:16:49,942 --> 00:16:52,042
I don't understand! You're too close to the camera, please!

327
00:16:52,042 --> 00:16:53,882
Just play your own style of shogi!

328
00:16:53,882 --> 00:16:56,742
Hey, you're better than this and you know it, Kiriyama!

329
00:16:56,962 --> 00:16:59,302
The Kato 4th Den are playing on the 4th floor!

330
00:16:59,582 --> 00:17:00,402
Don't you understand?

331
00:17:01,022 --> 00:17:04,082
He can't hear you. I have to say this is highly unusual!

332
00:17:04,642 --> 00:17:07,022
Hmm. I hope you're listening, kid.

333
00:17:07,502 --> 00:17:10,522
You've got a true-blue friend there who's really looking out for you.

334
00:17:11,302 --> 00:17:13,482
Yeah, wish I had friends like that.

335
00:17:13,802 --> 00:17:16,242
I'm only telling you this because we're best friends!

336
00:17:16,462 --> 00:17:17,822
You're best friend, he says!

337
00:17:17,822 --> 00:17:21,122
Ha-ha-ha! Youth, I'm jealous! All that energy!

338
00:17:22,222 --> 00:17:22,882
Oh, no!

339
00:17:23,302 --> 00:17:24,142
I don't know!

340
00:17:24,282 --> 00:17:26,142
Now listen! This is important!

341
00:17:26,562 --> 00:17:28,682
Uh, I'm only gonna say this once!

342
00:17:28,862 --> 00:17:32,882
In fact, I want you to get this on videotape and watch it over again and again!

343
00:17:33,322 --> 00:17:35,182
Oh, listen to that!

344
00:17:35,602 --> 00:17:37,162
Spoken like a true best friend.

345
00:17:37,242 --> 00:17:39,282
You've got to take better care of yourself!

346
00:17:40,022 --> 00:17:43,082
You're not making better progress because you don't do that!

347
00:17:43,082 --> 00:17:44,682
Damn it! What do you know?

348
00:17:44,862 --> 00:17:46,522
Who the hell do you think you are?

349
00:17:46,622 --> 00:17:48,262
You're messing me up, damn it!

350
00:17:48,522 --> 00:17:49,382
Hooray!

351
00:17:49,542 --> 00:17:51,562
Well, look at that! The kid is angry!

352
00:17:52,282 --> 00:17:54,722
What he's saying doesn't even make any sense!

353
00:17:54,922 --> 00:17:58,322
I'm only gonna say this once, so record it and watch it over and over!

354
00:17:58,542 --> 00:18:00,802
I don't even know what anything he says means!

355
00:18:01,262 --> 00:18:02,262
That's a good point.

356
00:18:02,642 --> 00:18:05,302
But I think Nikaido really does see you as his best friend.

357
00:18:05,462 --> 00:18:07,062
He really cares about you a lot.

358
00:18:07,422 --> 00:18:09,822
Wow! You guys are sweet and sour!

359
00:18:09,822 --> 00:18:12,822
There is still some hope for this generation after all!

360
00:18:13,082 --> 00:18:15,762
That was great!

361
00:18:15,922 --> 00:18:17,822
Huh? What was so great?

362
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:23,542
That was unexpected, Rei! You've never raised your voice!

363
00:18:24,862 --> 00:18:26,722
That wasn't what I expected.

364
00:18:29,242 --> 00:18:31,762
What she said actually surprised me.

365
00:18:33,642 --> 00:18:36,102
I want to learn! Shoggy looks fun!

366
00:18:37,582 --> 00:18:40,722
After all, no one's ever said that to me before.

367
00:18:41,542 --> 00:18:42,642
How could I respond?

368
00:18:43,082 --> 00:18:48,122
Do you think it would be alright if you taught me how to play?

369
00:18:59,922 --> 00:19:01,822
Would it be alright if you taught me how to play?

370
00:19:01,822 --> 00:19:04,502
What a surprise!

371
00:19:04,502 --> 00:19:07,782
No one had ever been that interested in my world before.

372
00:19:08,242 --> 00:19:09,842
It made me feel so happy.

373
00:19:10,842 --> 00:19:13,322
It was like swimming to shore for the first time.

374
00:19:13,682 --> 00:19:16,042
And with every breath, I felt even better.

375
00:19:16,042 --> 00:19:31,922
Maybe a plastic mat instead of a wooden board, since we'll probably be playing on the tea table in the living room.

376
00:19:35,922 --> 00:19:38,422
Maybe she should use these plastic pieces.

377
00:19:38,982 --> 00:19:40,302
They'll be easier for her to handle.

378
00:19:40,302 --> 00:19:43,182
Momo does often spill milk on the table.

379
00:19:47,182 --> 00:19:50,102
The characters won't wear off, so they'll be easy to read.

380
00:19:50,982 --> 00:19:53,642
Oh, and maybe a guide with pictures will help out too.

381
00:19:53,642 --> 00:19:57,122
I wonder, which one should I get?

382
00:19:57,322 --> 00:20:00,682
If you're looking for textbooks for a beginner, I can give you my recommendations.

383
00:20:03,162 --> 00:20:03,562
Mikaido?

384
00:20:04,522 --> 00:20:06,162
Darn, they're sold out of that one.

385
00:20:06,582 --> 00:20:07,462
How unfortunate.

386
00:20:07,462 --> 00:20:11,662
Um, I'll take this, please.

387
00:20:11,802 --> 00:20:12,742
You go, Kiriyama!

388
00:20:13,002 --> 00:20:15,282
You sense the importance of spreading the word, too!

389
00:20:17,122 --> 00:20:18,002
Sparkle, sparkle!

390
00:20:18,102 --> 00:20:19,322
So, who are you teaching?

391
00:20:21,602 --> 00:20:22,082
Wow!

392
00:20:22,642 --> 00:20:24,142
Thank you for all of your help!

393
00:20:24,422 --> 00:20:24,682
Yeah!

394
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:26,242
It's my pleasure!

395
00:20:26,482 --> 00:20:27,062
No problem!

396
00:20:29,142 --> 00:20:30,282
Okay, here goes.

397
00:20:30,482 --> 00:20:32,302
I hope I'll be able to remember everything.

398
00:20:32,782 --> 00:20:33,782
Don't even worry!

399
00:20:33,782 --> 00:20:38,742
It may look like it's hard to learn, but it's actually not that difficult when you first start out.

400
00:20:38,842 --> 00:20:41,622
If you do have trouble, just know that it's not your fault.

401
00:20:41,862 --> 00:20:46,602
It's your teacher that's fully responsible for how well you do and how well you learn, not you.

402
00:20:46,982 --> 00:20:48,642
And on that note...

403
00:20:48,642 --> 00:20:50,242
Over to you, Mr. Kiriyama!

404
00:20:50,402 --> 00:20:51,102
Go get him!

405
00:20:51,522 --> 00:20:53,462
It's my turn after leading like that?

406
00:20:53,582 --> 00:20:54,182
Come on!

407
00:20:57,262 --> 00:20:59,922
All right, I'll try to keep this as simple as I can.

408
00:20:59,922 --> 00:21:07,422
On this board with nine rows and nine columns, you and your opponent will each control 20 pieces that come in eight different types.

409
00:21:07,822 --> 00:21:11,902
You take turns getting each other's pieces with the objective of capturing the opponent's king.

410
00:21:12,342 --> 00:21:17,482
The person that's dubbed as black goes first, followed by the person playing as white, and then you continue going back and forth.

411
00:21:17,982 --> 00:21:21,542
Each of the eight types of pieces has its own attributes and range of movement.

412
00:21:22,102 --> 00:21:25,582
Also, the columns are called files and the rows are called ranks.

413
00:21:25,582 --> 00:21:28,202
Each column is numbered, as well as each row.

414
00:21:28,682 --> 00:21:31,122
Based on those numbers, all the boxes have addresses.

415
00:21:31,542 --> 00:21:33,882
Next, we'll learn about how each piece moves across the board.

416
00:21:34,882 --> 00:21:36,062
Kiriyama, slow down!

417
00:21:36,902 --> 00:21:38,682
Relax! You're too stiff, man!

418
00:21:41,082 --> 00:21:43,502
Look at her expression! She feels overwhelmed!

419
00:21:43,922 --> 00:21:45,302
Maybe this is too hard for me.

420
00:21:45,482 --> 00:21:47,922
You're gonna end up making her so nervous she won't get it!

421
00:21:48,082 --> 00:21:50,322
It'll all just go in one ear and out the other!

422
00:21:51,082 --> 00:21:52,702
You don't want to blow this chance!

423
00:21:52,702 --> 00:21:56,082
Her first impression has to be that it's easy to play!

424
00:21:56,582 --> 00:21:58,842
Okay, fine! Then what do you think I should do?

425
00:22:00,182 --> 00:22:01,842
All right! Listen up, ladies!

426
00:22:04,222 --> 00:22:06,302
It's my turn to teach you about Shogi!

427
00:22:07,502 --> 00:22:10,002
Hey! Let's look at this picture book together!

428
00:22:10,802 --> 00:22:11,582
All right!

429
00:22:11,582 --> 00:22:12,302
Meow-meow!

430
00:22:12,302 --> 00:22:12,382
Meow-meow!

431
00:22:12,382 --> 00:22:12,922
Meow-meow!

432
00:22:17,922 --> 00:22:19,762
Look, you kitty cat!

433
00:22:19,962 --> 00:22:21,182
There's also a king!

434
00:22:21,462 --> 00:22:23,002
And all kinds of kitties!

435
00:22:23,382 --> 00:22:26,422
Shogi is a board game in which you use eight different types of pieces.

436
00:22:26,662 --> 00:22:28,202
Each of them has its own personality.

437
00:22:28,502 --> 00:22:30,602
You win the game by capturing your opponent's king.

438
00:22:31,002 --> 00:22:34,382
You play on a board with 81 squares, 9 rows, and 9 columns.

439
00:22:34,842 --> 00:22:37,102
The three rows closest to you are your land.

440
00:22:37,102 --> 00:22:40,142
And the three rows on the other side are your opponent's land.

441
00:22:40,442 --> 00:22:44,662
Next, I'll introduce the personalities and abilities of each type of cat on the board.

442
00:22:44,862 --> 00:22:46,842
Daddy! I can't wait!

443
00:22:47,082 --> 00:22:48,462
Great! Let's continue!

444
00:22:49,602 --> 00:22:50,082
Nikaido!

445
00:22:50,542 --> 00:22:52,042
Why are you so good at this?

446
00:22:52,682 --> 00:22:55,642
What is this strange feeling I have?

447
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:36,651
Wow, really? No way! That's amazing!

448
00:24:36,651 --> 00:24:38,151
What the heck?!

449
00:24:38,151 --> 00:24:40,711
Young Master, this is lovely!

450
00:24:40,711 --> 00:24:44,151
Ah, Nikardo! You're one of the few good ones!

451
00:24:44,151 --> 00:24:47,551
I think I'm crying! I'm surprised you even noticed!

452
00:24:47,551 --> 00:24:50,371
My pawpads is gonna not do silly!

453
00:24:51,971 --> 00:24:54,571
Watch the next march comes in like a lion!

454
00:24:54,571 --> 00:24:58,131
Shogi is so much fun! Let's all try it together!

455
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:02,391
...

456
00:25:07,391 --> 00:25:08,391
...

457
00:25:08,631 --> 00:25:10,691
...

458
00:25:10,691 --> 00:25:15,631
...

459
00:25:15,631 --> 00:25:22,111
...

460
00:25:24,631 --> 00:25:26,671
...

461
00:25:28,271 --> 00:25:28,911
...

